{"name":"Cherry Hill","hex":"#cc5160","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cherry Hill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States:\nAn unincorporated community in Perry County, Arkansas.\nAn unincorporated community in Polk County, Arkansas.\nA neighbourhood in south Baltimore, Maryland.\nAn unincorporated community in Cecil County, Maryland.\nAn unincorporated community and historic district in Canton Township, Wayne County, Michigan.\nA township in Camden County, New Jersey. \nA hamlet in Harmony, Chautauqua County, New York.\nA neighbourhood of Roanoke, Virginia.\nA neighbourhood of Seattle, Washington.","An unincorporated community in Perry County, Arkansas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cherry_Hill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry Hill, New Jersey","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Hill is a township within Camden County, in the U.S. state of New Jersey. As a suburb of Philadelphia, the township is part of South Jersey and the Philadelphia metropolitan area. Cherry Hill grew during the mid-20th century suburbanization, becoming one of the Delaware Valley's main commercial centers, including the Cherry Hill Mall. As of the 2020 United States census, the township's population was 74,553."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Cherry_Hill%2C_NJ_municipal_building%2C_Nov._2025.jpg/330px-Cherry_Hill%2C_NJ_municipal_building%2C_Nov._2025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Hill%2C_New_Jersey"},{"title":"Cherry Hill, Prince William County, Virginia","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Hill is a census-designated place (CDP) in Prince William County, Virginia, United States. The population was 16,000 according to the 2010 Census. As of the 2020 census, it was estimated to be 23,683. The CDP is made up of the Cherry Hill peninsula, to the northeast of the town of Dumfries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Prince_William_County_Virginia_incorporated_and_unincorporated_areas_Cherry_Hill_highlighted.svg/330px-Prince_William_County_Virginia_incorporated_and_unincorporated_areas_Cherry_Hill_highlighted.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Hill%2C_Prince_William_County%2C_Virginia"},{"title":"Cherry","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry is the fruit of many plants of the genus Prunus, and is a fleshy drupe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg/330px-Cherry_season_%2848216568227%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry"},{"title":"Hill","blocks":[{"text":"A hill is a landform that extends above the surrounding terrain. It often has a distinct summit, and is usually applied to peaks which are above elevation compared to the relative landmass, though not as prominent as mountains. Hills fall under the category of slope landforms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG/330px-Uliveti_monte_cinto.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hill"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/45/Cherry_Hill%2C_NJ_seal.gif/120px-Cherry_Hill%2C_NJ_seal.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/45/Cherry_Hill%2C_NJ_seal.gif/250px-Cherry_Hill%2C_NJ_seal.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/45/Cherry_Hill%2C_NJ_seal.gif/120px-Cherry_Hill%2C_NJ_seal.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACherry_Hill%2C_NJ_sea